PS+=['【AAA News　March 17, 2021】\nOn the morning of March 16, Abu, a patas monkey (紅猴), ran away from Mountain Zoo. It happened at 11:30 am, when the zookeeper (動物園管理員) Henry Davis opened the gate of the monkey pen (圍欄) to clean it. Forba, a six-year-old patas monkey, ran out of the pen. Trying to get Forba back to the pen, Davis didn’t keep an eye on Abu, so Abu was able to get away from the pen. Forba was back, but Abu ran away. Davis reported it to the zoo at 11:35 am, but it was too late. Abu was out of the zoo and ran into the mountains.\nHere is a picture of Abu.（照片）Abu: 8 years old／83 cm／10 kg／good at climbing trees\nIf anyone sees Abu, please call Mountain Zoo.\nMountain Zoo　235 Beach Road, Beach Town　Phone: 6678-8890\n【Comments (回應)】\nLucy (10:04 am, March 17, 2021): Come on! Another animal got free from Mountain Zoo this month! What’s wrong with the zoo?\nRonald (10:35 am, March 17, 2021): I saw Abu in the mountains at about 7:15 this morning! When I saw it, it ran and hid behind a tree. I didn’t get close to it. I just walked away.\nJack (11:12 am, March 17, 2021): I worry about Abu. Can it find enough food in the mountains?\nMichelle (1:16 pm, March 17, 2021): Where is Abu now? Can it be dangerous? Why did Mountain Zoo make a big mistake like this?']
